{% comment %}
  Renders the body of the add-to-cart drawer: current cart contents, an
  optional cross-sell suggestion, and the checkout actions.

  Cross-sell rules are the "cross_sell_rule" metaobjects themselves — every
  ACTIVE entry, no theme step. Saving a rule is what makes it live, and its
  Status is what turns it off. (The theme setting is kept as a fallback for a
  definition without storefront access; see the region below.) Order comes
  from an optional `priority` number, lowest first, and the first rule that
  matches wins. A rule matches when:
  - its suggested product is not already in the cart
  - its domain list is empty or contains the current subdomain code
  - its "cart contains" list is empty or one of those products is in the cart
  - none of its "cart must not contain" products are in the cart
  - at least one variant of the suggested product is purchasable in the
    current domain's warehouse

  Rendered by sections/cart-notification-product.liquid on every add-to-cart
  (Section Rendering API), so the cart and rule evaluation are always fresh.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  # Which market's shelf answers "is this in stock". Markets moved from
  # subdomains to subfolders, so the code comes from the URL prefix
  # ("/en-kr" -> "kr") and the bare domain is the primary market. Read off
  # request.host, as this did, every market resolved to 'main' and the
  # cross-sell was answered for the international shelf: strips out of stock
  # in Korea were offered to a Korean customer, and strips out of stock on
  # 'main' were withheld from the ten markets that had them. A legacy
  # subdomain hostname still resolves, so an old rule keeps working if such a
  # domain is hit. Same resolution as stock-state.liquid and
  # delivery-date-buttons.liquid.
  assign host_clean = request.host | downcase | remove: 'www.'
  assign domain_code = 'main'
  if routes.root_url != '/'
    assign domain_code = routes.root_url | remove_first: '/' | split: '-' | last | downcase
  else
    assign host_parts = host_clean | split: '.'
    if host_parts.size > 2
      assign domain_code = host_parts | first
    endif
  endif

  assign current_wh = ''
  assign default_wh = ''
  assign wh_open = false
  assign default_wh_open = false
  for wh in settings.warehouses
    assign wh_loc = wh.location.value | strip | downcase
    if wh_loc == blank
      continue
    endif
    if wh.is_default.value and default_wh == ''
      assign default_wh = wh_loc
      if wh.sell_regardless.value
        assign default_wh_open = true
      endif
    endif
    if wh.domains.value
      for d in wh.domains.value
        assign dd = d | strip | downcase
        if dd == domain_code or dd == host_clean
          # Cleared and reset together — see stock-state.liquid. Two entries
          # claiming one market must not split the location from the tick.
          assign current_wh = wh_loc
          assign wh_open = false
          if wh.sell_regardless.value
            assign wh_open = true
          endif
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endfor
  if current_wh == ''
    assign current_wh = default_wh
    assign wh_open = default_wh_open
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%} xsell-rule-start
  Everything to the end marker is WHICH RULE WINS, and nothing else — no
  markup. `docs/spikes/cross-sell-rule-check.mjs` renders exactly this region
  in liquidjs against scripted rules and carts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign cs_rule = false -%}
{%- assign cs_product = false -%}
{%- assign cs_available_ids = '' -%}

{%- liquid
  # WHERE THE RULES COME FROM.
  #
  # They used to come from a theme setting — a metaobject_list somebody had to
  # add each new rule to in Theme settings > Cart Cross-sell. Creating the
  # entry under Content > Metaobjects did nothing on its own, which is a step
  # that is easy to half-do and impossible to see the absence of: the rule
  # looks finished, says Active, and never shows.
  #
  # So the rules are read straight off the metaobjects, as the popup versions
  # already are. The definition's publishable capability then means what it
  # says on the entry: ACTIVE entries are what `values` returns, so Status IS
  # the switch and a rule is live the moment it is saved.
  #
  # The setting stays as a FALLBACK, for one reason: `metaobjects.<type>` only
  # answers where the definition has storefront access, and a definition that
  # has not been granted it returns nothing at all. Falling back means the
  # worst case is the behaviour we already had rather than a cart drawer that
  # silently stopped suggesting anything. The comment below says which source
  # was used, so which one is in play is readable from outside.
  assign cs_pool = metaobjects.cross_sell_rule.values
  assign cs_source = 'metaobjects'
  if cs_pool == blank or cs_pool.size == 0
    assign cs_pool = settings.cross_sell_rules
    assign cs_source = 'setting'
  endif
-%}

{%- if cart != empty -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    First match wins, so ORDER matters. The setting's order was the priority;
    a metaobject list has no order of its own, so an optional `priority`
    number on the entry carries it — 1 first. The walk is one pass per rank
    and a final pass for everything unranked, which is how the popup section
    orders its versions, and for the same reason: Liquid cannot sort on a
    field inside a metaobject.

    With no `priority` field on the definition every rule is unranked and the
    order is whatever Shopify hands back. That is fine while no two rules can
    match one basket; add the field the day two can.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- for cs_pass in (1..13) -%}
  {%- for rule in cs_pool -%}
    {%- if cs_rule != false -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign cs_pri = rule.priority.value | default: 0 | plus: 0
      if cs_pass == 13
        # the last pass takes everything nobody ranked
        if cs_pri > 0
          continue
        endif
      else
        if cs_pri != cs_pass
          continue
        endif
      endif
    -%}
    {%- assign sp = rule.suggested_product.value -%}
    {%- if sp == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      # domain filter (empty list = all domains)
      assign domain_ok = true
      if rule.domains.value and rule.domains.value.size > 0
        assign domain_ok = false
        for d in rule.domains.value
          assign dd = d | strip | downcase
          if dd == domain_code or dd == host_clean
            assign domain_ok = true
          endif
        endfor
      endif
    -%}
    {%- unless domain_ok -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}

    {%- liquid
      # never suggest something already in the cart
      assign in_cart = false
      for item in cart.items
        if item.product_id == sp.id
          assign in_cart = true
        endif
      endfor
    -%}
    {%- if in_cart -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      # cart must contain one of these (empty = any basket)
      assign contains_ok = true
      if rule.cart_contains.value and rule.cart_contains.value.size > 0
        assign contains_ok = false
        for rp in rule.cart_contains.value
          for item in cart.items
            if item.product_id == rp.id
              assign contains_ok = true
            endif
          endfor
        endfor
      endif
    -%}
    {%- unless contains_ok -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}

    {%- liquid
      # cart must not contain any of these
      assign clash = false
      if rule.cart_not_contains.value and rule.cart_not_contains.value.size > 0
        for bp in rule.cart_not_contains.value
          for item in cart.items
            if item.product_id == bp.id
              assign clash = true
            endif
          endfor
        endfor
      endif
    -%}
    {%- if clash -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      # keep only variants purchasable in this warehouse
      assign avail_ids = ''
      for variant in sp.variants
        capture v_ok
          render 'warehouse-variant-available', variant: variant, parent: sp, current_wh: current_wh, wh_open: wh_open
        endcapture
        if v_ok contains 'true'
          assign avail_ids = avail_ids | append: variant.id | append: ','
        endif
      endfor
    -%}
    {%- if avail_ids == '' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

    {%- assign cs_rule = rule -%}
    {%- assign cs_product = sp -%}
    {%- assign cs_available_ids = avail_ids -%}
    {%- break -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} xsell-rule-end {%- endcomment -%}

<!-- cross-sell: source={{ cs_source }} rules={{ cs_pool | size }} [{% for r in cs_pool %}{{ r.system.handle }}{% unless forloop.last %} {% endunless %}{% endfor %}] matched={% if cs_product %}{{ cs_product.handle }}{% else %}none{% endif %} warehouse={{ current_wh | default: 'unmapped' }} -->


<div class="cart-drawer__scroll">
  {%- if cart == empty -%}
    <div class="cart-drawer__empty">
      <p class="cart-drawer__empty-text">{{ 'sections.cart.empty' | t }}</p>
      <button type="button" class="button button--primary" data-drawer-close>
        {{ 'general.continue_shopping' | t }}
      </button>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="cart-drawer__items">
    {%- for item in cart.items -%}
      <div class="cart-drawer__item" data-line-key="{{ item.key }}" data-quantity="{{ item.quantity }}">
        {%- if item.image -%}
          <img
            class="cart-drawer__item-image"
            src="{{ item.image | img_url: '200x' }}"
            alt="{{ item.image.alt | escape }}"
            width="100"
            height="{{ 100 | divided_by: item.image.aspect_ratio | ceil }}"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
        <div class="cart-drawer__item-info">
          <p class="cart-drawer__item-title">{{ item.product.title | escape }}</p>
          {%- unless item.product.has_only_default_variant -%}
            {%- for option in item.options_with_values -%}
              <p class="cart-drawer__item-meta">{{ option.value | escape }}</p>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endunless -%}
          {%- assign dd_prop = item.properties['Delivery Date'] -%}
          {%- if dd_prop != blank -%}
            <p class="cart-drawer__item-meta">{{ 'delivery.date_title' | t }}: {{ dd_prop | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="cart-drawer__item-qty">
            <button type="button" class="cart-drawer__qty-btn" data-qty-change="-1" aria-label="{{ 'products.product.quantity.decrease' | t: product: item.product.title | escape }}">&minus;</button>
            <span class="cart-drawer__qty-value" aria-live="polite">{{ item.quantity }}</span>
            <button type="button" class="cart-drawer__qty-btn" data-qty-change="1" aria-label="{{ 'products.product.quantity.increase' | t: product: item.product.title | escape }}">+</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cart-drawer__item-side">
          <p class="cart-drawer__item-price">
            <span>{{ item.final_line_price | money }}</span>
            {%- if item.original_line_price > item.final_line_price -%}
              <s>{{ item.original_line_price | money }}</s>
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>
          <button type="button" class="cart-drawer__remove" data-qty-remove>{{ 'general.cart.remove' | t }}</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>

  {%- if cs_product -%}
    {%- assign inherit_date = cart.items.first.properties['Delivery Date'] -%}
    {%- assign pct = cs_rule.discount_percent.value | default: 0 | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- assign price_factor = 100 | minus: pct -%}

    {%- liquid
      assign default_variant = false
      for variant in cs_product.variants
        assign id_needle = variant.id | append: ','
        if cs_available_ids contains id_needle and default_variant == false
          assign default_variant = variant
        endif
      endfor
      assign default_disc = default_variant.price | times: price_factor | divided_by: 100
    -%}

    <aside
      class="drawer-upsell"
      data-cross-sell
      {% if inherit_date != blank %}data-delivery-date="{{ inherit_date | escape }}"{% endif %}
    >
      <p class="drawer-upsell__headline">{{ cs_rule.headline.value | default: cs_product.title }}</p>

      {%- if cs_rule.benefit.value != blank -%}
        <p class="drawer-upsell__benefit">{{ cs_rule.benefit.value }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="cart-drawer__item drawer-upsell__row">
        {%- assign cs_image = default_variant.featured_image | default: cs_product.featured_image -%}
        {%- if cs_image -%}
          <a href="{{ cs_product.url }}" class="drawer-upsell__media" data-cross-sell-link>
            <img
              class="cart-drawer__item-image"
              data-cross-sell-image
              src="{{ cs_image | img_url: '200x' }}"
              alt="{{ cs_image.alt | escape }}"
              width="100"
              height="{{ 100 | divided_by: cs_image.aspect_ratio | ceil }}"
              loading="lazy"
            >
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="cart-drawer__item-info">
          <a href="{{ cs_product.url }}" class="cart-drawer__item-title drawer-upsell__title-link" data-cross-sell-link>{{ cs_product.title | escape }}</a>
          <p class="drawer-upsell__price">
            <span data-cross-sell-price>{{ default_disc | money }}</span>
            {%- if pct > 0 -%}
              <s data-cross-sell-compare>{{ default_variant.price | money }}</s>
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>

          {%- if cs_product.has_only_default_variant -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="cross-sell-variant" value="{{ default_variant.id }}">
          {%- else -%}
            <select
              class="drawer-upsell__variant-select"
              name="cross-sell-variant"
              aria-label="{{ cs_product.options_with_values.first.name | escape }}"
            >
              {%- for variant in cs_product.variants -%}
                {%- assign id_needle = variant.id | append: ',' -%}
                {%- if cs_available_ids contains id_needle -%}
                  {%- assign v_disc = variant.price | times: price_factor | divided_by: 100 -%}
                  <option
                    value="{{ variant.id }}"
                    data-price="{{ v_disc | money }}"
                    {% if pct > 0 %}data-compare="{{ variant.price | money }}"{% endif %}
                    {% if variant.featured_image %}data-image="{{ variant.featured_image | img_url: '200x' }}"{% endif %}
                    {% if variant.id == default_variant.id %}selected{% endif %}
                  >
                    {{- variant.title | escape -}}
                  </option>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </select>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <div class="cart-drawer__item-side">
          <button type="button" class="drawer-upsell__add" data-cross-sell-add>
            {{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- if cart != empty -%}
  <div class="cart-drawer__footer">
    <div class="cart-drawer__totals">
      <div class="cart-drawer__totals-row">
        <span>{{ 'general.cart.shipping' | t }}</span>
        <span class="cart-drawer__totals-muted">{{ 'general.cart.calculated_at_checkout' | t }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cart-drawer__totals-row">
        <span>{{ 'general.cart.total' | t }}</span>
        <span>{{ cart.total_price | money_with_currency }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <form action="{{ routes.cart_url }}" method="post">
      <button class="button button--primary button--full-width" name="checkout">
        {{ 'sections.cart.checkout' | t }}
      </button>
    </form>

  </div>
{%- endif -%}
